@startuml
title Defense Core — Deterministic Validation, Routing, Retry, and Terminal Activity
skinparam shadowing false

start
:Receive workflow definition,
mode, and named deterministic scenario;
:Validate exactly one designated start;
:Validate at least one reachable terminal
and every task reachable from start;
:Reject self-edge or directed cycle;
:Accept only SUCCESS, FAILURE, ALWAYS;
:Reject equal-precedence ambiguity;
:Validate every task has a positive
maximum-total-attempt bound;

if (Complete definition valid?) then (no)
  :Reject definition with violations;
  :Create no run, attempt, retry,
  transition-selection, or trace state;
  stop
else (yes)
  :Create isolated run and persist initial trace;
  :Set current task to designated start;
endif

while (Run has no terminal state?) is (continue)
  :Take next deterministic scenario outcome
  for current task;
  :Persist attempt ordinal and outcome
  in run-local trace order;

  if (Outcome is FAILURE?) then (yes)
    if (Completed attempts < positive bound?) then (yes)
      :Persist retry observation;
      :Keep current task unchanged;
      note right
      Retry repeats the current task.
      No transition is selected or traversed.
      Bound 1 permits zero retries.
      end note
    else (no — bound reached)
      :Do not retry;
      :Resolve final FAILURE normally;
      if (Matching FAILURE transition exists?) then (yes)
        :Select matching FAILURE transition;
        :Persist selection before advancement;
        :Set current task to selected target;
      else (no)
        if (ALWAYS fallback exists?) then (yes)
          :Select ALWAYS fallback;
          :Persist selection before advancement;
          :Set current task to selected target;
        else (no)
          :Persist unsuccessful terminal state
          and terminal trace observation together;
          stop
        endif
      endif
    endif
  else (SUCCESS)
    :Resolve final SUCCESS normally;
    if (Matching SUCCESS transition exists?) then (yes)
      :Select matching SUCCESS transition;
      :Persist selection before advancement;
      :Set current task to selected target;
    else (no)
      if (ALWAYS fallback exists?) then (yes)
        :Select ALWAYS fallback;
        :Persist selection before advancement;
        :Set current task to selected target;
      else (no)
        :Persist successful terminal state
        and terminal trace observation together;
        stop
      endif
    endif
  endif
endwhile (terminal)

stop

legend
Status: APPROVED — checkpoint 4 architecture baseline
Requirements baseline: 6074fd7ef490ea3b08177e7a786035159f39a91c
Working base: b5c7da9e51382bb418f017790ae944c8dff26a06
Implementation: NOT STARTED
Executable verification: NOT STARTED
Release: NOT SCHEDULED
Both modes use this one accepted checkpoint-4 semantic algorithm.
Equal-precedence ambiguity is rejected during validation, not resolved here.
endlegend
@enduml
